# Options of the GNSS bike computer itself (NCS v3.3.0).
#
# The application Kconfig has to source the Zephyr one at the end, as the
# Zephyr application development guide describes.

menu "GNSS bike computer"

config GNSS_ROUTE_POINTS
	int "Points of a route kept in memory"
	default 500
	range 100 16000
	help
	  A route of the rider (a `.PAR` of the legacy, or a course exported
	  from Strava or Komoot) is read into a static array of this many
	  points, sixteen bytes each. A file with more points is halved as it
	  loads, so the whole route always fits, with less resolution: a
	  hundred kilometres over 500 points leaves one point every 200 m,
	  and over 4000 one every 25 m, which is what the services export.

	  The board with 512 KB of RAM can afford the larger number; the
	  nRF52840 of the old board cannot.

config GNSS_SEGMENT_POINTS
	int "Points of a segment kept in memory"
	default 256
	range 64 4000
	help
	  Each of the three segments that can be loaded at the same time
	  holds this many points, sixteen bytes each, and a longer file is
	  halved as it loads. The longest segment of `tools/TDD/DB` has 1291
	  points.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
